Repository: https://github.com/LaurenzV/hayro (crate hayro-jbig2)
Base: ea9c81dc70cde40c64205986fdcfcd481fe934d8
Fork: https://github.com/close2/hayro

The base is hayro-jbig2 0.3.1: upstream tags the commit `hayro-jbig2-v0.3.1`, the published
crate's `.cargo_vcs_info.json` names it, and its `src/` is byte for byte the published one. The
root Cargo.toml pins the three hayro codecs to upstream's repository at that commit (ADR 1714). The
paths below are the repository's, so the patch applies at its root with `git apply`. The owner
applies this to the fork on that base, pushes, and moves the three stanzas to the fork at the
pushed commit; `tools/state.sh main-checkout` lists it until then.

